<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalNotDisjoint> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "This relation is the complement of intervalDisjoint and is the disjoint union of intervalEquals, intervalWhollyContains, intervalWhollyContainedBy, intervalOverlaps, intervalOverlappedBy. However, that is outside OWL-2 expressivity, so is implemented as an explicit property, with intervalEquals, intervalWhollyContains, intervalWhollyContainedBy, intervalOverlaps, intervalOverlappedBy as sub-properties"@en .
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalNotDisjoint> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "If T1 :intervalNotDisjoint T2, then the two entities overlap or coincide in some way, but their ordering relationship is not known."@en .
