<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalEquals> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "If T1 :intervalEquals T2, then the beginning of T1 is coincident with the beginning of T2, and the end of T1 is coincident with the end of T2, and the beginning of T1 is not concident with the end of T1."@en .
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalEquals> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "intervalo igual"@es .
