<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalOverlaps> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "If T1 :intervalOverlaps T2, then the beginning of T1 is before the beginning of T2, the end of T1 is after the beginning of T2, and the end of T1 is before the end of T2."@en .
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalOverlaps> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "intervalo se solapa"@es .
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalOverlaps> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Si un intervalo propio T1 se solapa con otro intervalo propio T2, entonces el principio de T1 es anterior al principio de T2, el final de T1 es posterior al principio de T2, y el final de T1 es anterior al final de T2."@es .
<http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalOverlaps> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalOverlappedBy> .
